# Hardening watch orchestrator — OPTIONAL agent-invocation config.
#
# Copy to `scripts/hardening-watch.env` (gitignored) to let the watcher AUTO-INVOKE the next
# agent in --run-once / --interval. If unset, the watcher runs in supervised MANUAL mode: it
# tells you which agent + packet to run, you run it, then re-run the watcher. Both are valid.
#
# Templates support placeholders: {{TASK_FILE}} {{AGENT}} {{WAVE}}
# The command MUST: read the packet, do the work, commit (docs/approved scope), and update the
# handoff files (next_agent, log, next packet). The watcher validates the result afterwards.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ENVIRONMENT NOTE (checked 2026-06-29): no agent CLI was found on this machine —
#   • Cursor: no `cursor-agent` / `cursor` CLI  → Cursor steps are MANUAL (run in the IDE).
#   • Claude: no working `claude` CLI on PATH    → Claude steps are MANUAL (run in chat).
# Leave these unset until a working CLI is installed + permission flags verified. Auto-invoke
# of an agent that edits files needs non-interactive permissions — verify on a first --run-once
# before trusting it, and never enable --interval/overnight until --run-once is proven.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Cursor execution agent (example — only if you install a Cursor agent CLI):
# HARDENING_CURSOR_CMD=cursor-agent --file {{TASK_FILE}}

# Claude review/plan agent (example — Claude Code headless print mode, if `claude` is on PATH):
# HARDENING_CLAUDE_CMD=claude -p "$(cat {{TASK_FILE}})" --permission-mode acceptEdits
